      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 10**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.storybook/preview.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-3`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**Storybook에도 전역 스타일을 같이 주입해 렌더링 차이를 줄여주세요.**\n\n현재는 `ThemeProvider`만 적용되어 앱(`src/App.tsx`)과 스토리의 기본 스타일 조건이 달라질 수 있습니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>변경 예시</summary>\n\n```diff\n import { ThemeProvider } from '@emotion/react';\n+import { Global } from '@emotion/react';\n import type { Preview } from '@storybook/react-vite';\n import { theme } from '../src/styles/theme';\n+import { globalStyles } from '../src/styles/globalStyles';\n\n ...\n     (Story) => (\n       <ThemeProvider theme={theme}>\n+        <Global styles={globalStyles} />\n         <Story />\n       </ThemeProvider>\n     ),\n```\n</details>\n\n \n\n\nAlso applies to: 22-25\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn @.storybook/preview.tsx around lines 1 - 3, The Storybook preview only wraps\nstories with ThemeProvider and misses the app's global styles; update\n.storybook/preview.tsx to also inject the app's global styles by importing and\napplying the same global CSS or Emotion Global component used by the app (e.g.,\nthe GlobalStyles component or global.css from src/styles) alongside\nThemeProvider so stories and src/App.tsx share identical base styles; ensure you\nreference and use the existing theme and the same global-style export (e.g.,\nGlobalStyles or a Global from '@emotion/react') when wrapping stories in\nPreview.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/types/cardStausTypes.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-6`: **`cardBrand` 타입을 지원되는 브랜드 집합으로 좁혀보세요.**\n\n현재 코드에서 `cardBrand`에 할당되는 값을 확인해보니 `''`, `'visa'`, `'master'` 세 가지뿐입니다(useCardNumber.tsx, CardPreview 등). `string` 타입이면 이 집합 밖의 값(예: 오타)이 런타임에 잠입할 수 있으므로, 실제 사용되는 값들을 기반으로 유니온 타입으로 정의하면 컴파일 타임에 미지원 값을 차단할 수 있습니다.\n\n현재 지원되는 브랜드들을 명시적 타입으로 표현하면 CardPreview.tsx의 조건부 로직도 더 안전해질 것입니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/types/cardStausTypes.ts` at line 6, Change the cardBrand property in the\nCardStatus type (in src/types/cardStausTypes.ts) from a general string to a\nunion of the actual supported values (e.g., '' | 'visa' | 'master') so only\nallowed brands can be assigned; update any code that imports/uses this type\n(useCardNumber.tsx, CardPreview.tsx) to satisfy the new type (adjust assignments\nor guards) so compile-time checks prevent unsupported values.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@index.html`:\n- Line 2: 현재 문서의 루트 html 요소(lang=\"en\")가 UI의 한국어 설정과 불일치하므로 <html> 태그의 lang 속성 값을\n\"en\"에서 \"ko\"로 변경하여 스크린리더와 검색엔진에 한국어 문서임을 정확히 알리세요; index.html 파일에서 \"<html\nlang=\"en\">\"을 찾아 lang=\"ko\"로 교체하면 됩니다.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardCvc.tsx`:\n- Around line 21-37: The label in CardCvc is not connected to the input; update\nthe CardCvc component so the <label> uses htmlFor with a unique id (e.g.,\n\"card-cvc\") and the <input> has the matching id; add accessibility attributes on\nthe input: set aria-invalid based on the component's error state (use whatever\nerror flag is on cardCvc or setCardCvc), and add aria-describedby pointing to an\nerror message element id (e.g., \"card-cvc-error\") that you render when there is\nan error; apply the same pattern to CardNumber and CardExpiryDate components\nreferencing their own ids and error message ids.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardInput.tsx`:\n- Around line 31-35: The form in the CardInput component currently has no\nonSubmit handler so pressing Enter can trigger a full page submit; update the\n<form> in CardInput (the component rendering CardNumber, CardExpiryDate,\nCardCvc) to either replace the <form> with a non-form container (e.g., <div>) or\nadd an onSubmit handler that calls event.preventDefault() (e.g., add\nonSubmit={(e) => e.preventDefault()} to the form) to stop default submission and\npreserve input state. Ensure you modify the JSX in CardInput.tsx where the form\nelement is rendered.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardNumber.tsx`:\n- Around line 31-67: The label element and the four inputs in CardNumber.tsx are\nnot programmatically associated, so update the rendering inside the\ncardStatus.cardNumbers.map loop to provide a unique accessible name for each\ninput (either add id on each input and link the top label via htmlFor to a\nwrapper/input, or add explicit aria-label/aria-labelledby values like \"카드번호 자리\n1\", \"카드번호 자리 2\", etc.); ensure the unique identifier references the index (e.g.,\nusing index to build the id or aria-label), keep existing props and handlers\n(setCardStatus.handleCardNumbers, handleCardNumbersBlur, value, maxLength), and\nmake sure any error styling/logic using cardStatus.cardNumberErrorMode continues\nto work after adding the id/aria attribute.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardPreview.tsx`:\n- Around line 41-43: The CardPreview component renders brand images (variables\nvisa and master) based on cardBrand but omits alt attributes; update the <img>\nelements in CardPreview to include meaningful alt text (e.g., alt={`Visa card\nlogo`} for visa and alt={`Mastercard logo`} for master) or use alt=\"\" if the\nimages are purely decorative, ensuring the alt reflects the cardBrand variable\nso assistive tech can convey the brand.\n- Around line 63-67: Guard accesses to cardNumbers[2] and cardNumbers[3] before\nusing .length to avoid runtime errors when those indexes are missing; update the\ntwo span renderings in CardPreview (the elements that repeat '·' based on\ncardNumbers[2].length and cardNumbers[3].length) to compute lengths safely\n(e.g., using a fallback or optional chaining such as treating missing entries as\nempty string) so the repeat count is always a number and cannot throw.\n\nIn `@src/hooks/useCardNumber.tsx`:\n- Around line 15-17: The current numeric check using isNotNumber(Number(...))\nallows things like \"+1\", \" 1\", and \"1e2\"; update the validation in useCardNumber\n(where isNotNumber(...) and setCardNumberErrorMode are used) to enforce\ndigits-only by testing the raw input string against a regex like /^[0-9]+$/\n(apply trim() if you want to reject leading/trailing spaces or omit trim() to\ntreat spaces as invalid), and change the early-return condition to call that\nregex (or update isNotNumber to use that regex) so only strings composed\nexclusively of characters 0-9 pass the card number validation.\n\nIn `@src/hooks/useExpiryDate.tsx`:\n- Around line 46-53: handleMonthBlur currently only checks for empty month and\nsets 'normal' for any non-empty value; enhance it to validate that\ncardExpiryDate[0] is exactly two digits and parses to an integer between 1 and\n12. On blur: if cardExpiryDate[0].length === 0\nsetCardExpiryDateErrorMode('emptyMonth'); else if cardExpiryDate[0].length !== 2\nor parsed month < 1 or > 12 setCardExpiryDateErrorMode('invalidMonth'); else\nsetCardExpiryDateErrorMode('normal'); use handleMonthBlur, cardExpiryDate and\nsetCardExpiryDateErrorMode to locate and implement this logic.\n\nIn `@src/stories/CardExpiryDate.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 25-29: The story mock is wrapping the spy with an empty arrow\nfunction so blur events never call the underlying spy; in the setCardExpiry\nobjects replace handleCardExpiryDate: () => fn(), handleYearBlur: () => fn(),\nhandleMonthBlur: () => fn() with the spy itself (e.g., handleCardExpiryDate: fn,\nhandleYearBlur: fn, handleMonthBlur: fn) so the real function is invoked on\nblur; make the same change for the other setCardExpiry mocks in this file (the\nrepeated blocks around the other stories).\n\nIn `@src/utils/util.ts`:\n- Around line 31-37: The isNotNumber function currently converts inputs with\nNumber(...) and relies on isNaN, allowing values like \" \", \"\" or \"1e2\" to pass;\nupdate isNotNumber to accept the raw input as a string (change its parameter\nsignature) and validate on the trimmed string rather than Number(...) — reject\nempty/whitespace-only strings and validate numeric format with a strict check\n(e.g., regex for allowed digit/decimal format or using parseFloat combined with\na pattern) before calling setFunc(errorMode); update all callers of isNotNumber\nto pass the original string input instead of a number so the new string-based\nvalidation is used consistently.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn @.storybook/preview.tsx:\n- Around line 1-3: The Storybook preview only wraps stories with ThemeProvider\nand misses the app's global styles; update .storybook/preview.tsx to also inject\nthe app's global styles by importing and applying the same global CSS or Emotion\nGlobal component used by the app (e.g., the GlobalStyles component or global.css\nfrom src/styles) alongside ThemeProvider so stories and src/App.tsx share\nidentical base styles; ensure you reference and use the existing theme and the\nsame global-style export (e.g., GlobalStyles or a Global from '@emotion/react')\nwhen wrapping stories in Preview.\n\nIn `@src/types/cardStausTypes.ts`:\n- Line 6: Change the cardBrand property in the CardStatus type (in\nsrc/types/cardStausTypes.ts) from a general string to a union of the actual\nsupported values (e.g., '' | 'visa' | 'master') so only allowed brands can be\nassigned; update any code that imports/uses this type (useCardNumber.tsx,\nCardPreview.tsx) to satisfy the new type (adjust assignments or guards) so\ncompile-time checks prevent unsupported values.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\